1
00:00:00,215 --> 00:00:01,525
(Penny:)Okay, I know you don't
want to talk about it,

2
00:00:01,683 --> 00:00:04,563
(Penny:)but can I just ask you one question
about your mom's book?

3
00:00:04,786 --> 00:00:06,896
(Amy:)-No.
-I just want to know

4
00:00:07,055 --> 00:00:09,225
(Penny:)why a five-year-old boy puts
on his mom's make-up

5
00:00:09,391 --> 00:00:11,371
(Penny:)and wears balloon boobies.

6
00:00:14,329 --> 00:00:16,669
(Leonard:)They weren't boobies.
They were muscles.

7
00:00:17,532 --> 00:00:20,742
(Leonard:)And the make-up was green.
I was pretending to be the Hulk.

8
00:00:21,536 --> 00:00:22,986
(Penny:)You were wearing her bra.

9
00:00:23,038 --> 00:00:24,208
(Leonard:)That was to keep my muscles
from sagging!

10
00:00:24,506 --> 00:00:26,646
(Leonard:)Can we please stop talking
about this?!

11
00:00:27,642 --> 00:00:30,422
(Penny:)Okay, okay. But you know,
as a student of psychology

12
00:00:30,645 --> 00:00:33,645
(Penny:)who got a check-plus on her
first homework assignment...

13
00:00:34,716 --> 00:00:37,756
(Penny:)I think, sometimes, it's good
to open up about these things.

14
00:00:37,919 --> 00:00:41,089
(Leonard:)Okay, fine. Do you want to know
why I dressed like the Hulk?

15
00:00:41,223 --> 00:00:42,893
(Leonard:)Because I was always mad at my mom

16
00:00:43,024 --> 00:00:44,934
(Leonard:)and I wanted to smash
my way out of that house.

17
00:00:45,393 --> 00:00:48,273
(Penny:)-Well, why were you so angry?
-Gee, I don't know.

18
00:00:48,597 --> 00:00:51,597
(Leonard:)Maybe it's because I was always
the subject of her little experiments.

19
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,610
(Leonard:)Did you get to the chapter
where she staged the Easter egg hunt

20
00:00:54,836 --> 00:00:57,616
(Leonard:)with no eggs to see how long
I'd keep looking?

21
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:03,020
The answer, by the way: June.

